WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.160
A winter afternoon, late in the day.

2
00:00:03.210 --> 00:00:06.250
A bare landscape, and nobody about.

3
00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:09.200
Low sunlight slants across the fields.

4
00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:11.320
Long shadows stretch.

5
00:00:11.370 --> 00:00:13.860
Faint organ music plays.

6
00:00:13.910 --> 00:00:17.480
"There's a certain slant
of light," the poem begins.

7
00:00:17.530 --> 00:00:20.680
And something about that
light troubles the speaker.

8
00:00:20.730 --> 00:00:21.720
No army.

9
00:00:21.770 --> 00:00:22.890
No enemy.

10
00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:25.360
So why is this a Conflict poem?

11
00:00:25.410 --> 00:00:29.840
In this mission, you'll find out what
this light does to the people who see it.

12
00:00:29.890 --> 00:00:32.500
You'll go looking for
the harm this light does.

13
00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:35.240
Where is it, and why can't anyone see it?

14
00:00:35.290 --> 00:00:40.620
And you'll meet a poet, Emily Dickinson,
whose poem was only printed in 1890,

15
00:00:40.670 --> 00:00:42.110
after her death.

16
00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:45.720
Your mission: explain why
this is a Conflict poem.
